  "interpretation": "⟨c⟩_β values give the Wedderburn-weighted average content for each atomic braid; the chirality first-order factor is a_K(β) = 1 + w(β) · ⟨c⟩_β · h where w(β) is the writhe and h = q − q⁻¹.  w(β) is a datum of the braid WORD at a fixed strand count, not of the closure — Markov II shifts it by ±1 — so a_K is well-defined only once the level is pinned.  Per the owner ruling the level is the braid index; the rows here record whether they sit at it.",
