    "invariant": "For n ≤ 3 the transpose pairing collapses the numerator exactly to (c_max/[n]_q!)·(q^ℓ − (−1/q)^ℓ), since dim_q((n)) = dim_q((1^n)) = 1 and the only non-extreme partition at n ≤ 3 is the self-transpose (2,1) with c = 0.  SIGN/POSITIVITY INVARIANT: for real q > 0, odd ℓ gives q^ℓ + q^{−ℓ} ≥ 2 > 0 (AM–GM, never zero) and even ℓ gives q^ℓ − q^{−ℓ}, zero only at q = 1.  Hence at q_0 ≠ 1, ⟨c⟩_β = 0 ⟺ writhe = 0. The cancellation therefore CANNOT deliver ≈ 0 for any nonzero-writhe braid at n ≤ 3.  Verified per row by transpose_collapse_check().",
